Z||000000||fierospeeder||06-06-2000||05:29 AM||||I recently purchased a micro fiche from ebay, and does anyone know how to get these on paper.  My dad works at wrigley gum, in the machine shop, and he said they use to have the machines to make copies onto paper, and they have updated to some other method.<P>Does someone like office max do this type of work?  Or will a photo scanner work?  I seen some people selling CD versions which you view with acrobat that has the fiche already been uploaded to a file, which i like to do, so i can send it to anyone on the internet.<P>thanks <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gokart||06-06-2000||05:42 AM||||I got my 22P P/I from Bell and Howell for $6.00 on microfiche and my wife is currently having them put on paper for me at the library. Not all librarys have a fiche reader so I'd call some first. It's alot of work as well. She's already spent at least an hour there and hasn't even gotten to the parts yet! I'm wishing I'd spent the money to just buy the printed version cause this may end up costing the same to have them printed out...maybe even more <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||2
