Z||000004||Terrybogin||06-08-2000||03:25 AM||||Some college libraries have the fiche readers that do not charge for making paper copies. You could also hang out at the surplus auctions and buy your own microfiche reader. At the last auction I went to, one sold for $5.00 because nobody knew what to do with it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||06-10-2000||04:24 PM||||Any good scanner that can read transparancies should work. You need something with high optical resolution, not one that uses electonic enhancement to fake higher resolution than it really has. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Rodrv6||06-10-2000||10:53 PM||||Be careful not to smoke around your microfiche-----unless you like smoked fiche! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000007||gixxer||06-11-2000||04:56 PM||||We have one at work that makes paper copies. How many cards do you have? ||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierospeeder||06-12-2000||02:27 AM||||i have two of them i like to do,<BR>one of a nighthawk 550<BR>and a vw beetle <P>the nighthawk is about a 4X7  50 pages <BR>the beetle is a 8X10 i think its about 200 pages if you print it out<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||gixxer||06-12-2000||07:45 PM||||Hang on speeder, I'm not really microfiche literate. I gotta see what the capability of our machines are. One machine takes a single card at a time with one drawing embedded in the middle of it. The other machine takes a sort of plastic casette, that you can wind/rewind. Both have print out capability. What have you got?<BR>250 pages! I fell uncomfortable about this already.<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000010||fierospeeder||06-12-2000||10:14 PM||||the honda nighthawk <BR>is about the size of a 4X7 <BR>it has about 50 small images on one film.<BR>so after printing out all the images, the result should be 50 images.<P>the vw beetle 74, is one sheet of film of a size about 8X10.  It has about 200 images on that single sheet.  When you print it out, your going to get about 200 pages.||||reg||1
